# Fuzzing & invariant testing

Method: `methodology/INVARIANT-METHODOLOGY.md`. Foundry specifics:
`integrations/foundry/README.md`.

- Every invariant in `.security/invariants.yaml` needs at least one
  `invariant_*` stateful test; the campaign is recorded via
  `security-check SEC-TEST-003`.
- Use handler contracts: constrain the fuzzer to valid-but-adversarial
  sequences; track ghost totals for the invariant to compare against. Never
  constrain so tightly that attacks become unreachable — the handler must
  allow multiple actors, reentrant callers, and boundary amounts.
- Fuzz tests (`testFuzz_*`) for single-function properties: round-trip
  non-profitability, monotonicity, bounds.
- When a campaign finds a counterexample: FIRST freeze it as an
  `exploit_regression` test in `test/exploits/`, THEN fix, so the fix is
  proven against the real sequence.
- Campaign parameters (runs/depth in `foundry.toml`) are part of the
  evidence; do not lower them to make a slow failure disappear.
